  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the seed decides every kernel Map <-> FinitelySupportedFunction position by the declaration it resolves to -- the join through v1.compiler.infer_env settled_type (#15118), the crossing through one declared ConversionPlan pair beside literal_homomorphism_rows, and every remaining leaf-spelling probe named in the FOLLOW-UP receipt below -- each executed RED keyed by declaration so a look-alike leaf named Map does not match" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the leaf name Map stands for two representations of one concept. std.types Map is std.algebra FinitelySupportedFunction; a Map<K,V> annotation in a module that imports nothing defining Map (std.algebra) resolves to the KERNEL Map, host-realized. Several seed sites decide by the last name segment Map, so the two are told apart, or conflated, by spelling rather than by the declaration a position resolves to (DESIGN section 4, kernel_map_is_the_host_realization_of_the_finitely_supported_function; the Map instance of text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold).",
    "HARM: retyping the std.algebra map surface to FinitelySupportedFunction fails seed typecheck at the if-join with 'if branches resolve to incompatible types: FinitelySupportedFunction<String,X> vs Map' (scratch/algebra-map-fsf 27bda760a8, BuildBuddy 35e3f094-c706-497f-a642-7a07d75f4f20), and Map is unbound at the std.algebra resolve wall (std.keyed_row/keyed_roster infer gate). No diagnostic names the crossing: the refusal is a type-shape mismatch, not a located refusal of an undeclared crossing.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: native v2 keys Map by declaration path (v2.std.map_introduction), so the class is seed-side. The three *_primitive_delegate seams in std.algebra are where the host operation is bound; their primitive_projection rows key on declaration name, not type. Not an instance of the text class: the carrier is a value crossing between two collection declarations, with no literal.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (no rung of the ladder guarantees a value crossing between two representations of one concept is refused unless a row declares it; the wall that decides it is a bare name comparison). CEILING: structurally guaranteed (decidable once the classifier reads the resolved declaration at every position). NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the Map ConversionPlan pair beside unicode_scalar_unfold/fold in gunbc.structural_realization_bindings (the same carrier, not a new mechanism; total because FinitelySupportedFunction is declared as a fn-backed total surface over a finite support and the kernel Map's host map IS that support -- one host operation, v1_rt's map helpers, bound through the *_primitive_delegate seams; exact because the pair's endpoints name the two declarations, never the leaf name); plus an executed RED (undeclared kernel Map <-> FinitelySupportedFunction use refuses with a typed, located diagnostic naming the missing crossing) and a positive control through the declared plan.",
    "FOLLOW-UP (named, not silent; the sibling leaves of the join rule #15118 fixed -- DESIGN 6b, 'consolidate duplicate answers'): seed judgments still key on the leaf spelling Map and must be keyed by declaration identity. THE CENSUS IS AN IDENTITY JOIN OVER A STATED POPULATION, NOT A COUNT EQUALITY (DESIGN section 5). Review 86783 caught four named against six claimed; review 87351 caught a named site that does not exist and a hand count wrong again; review 87479 caught this file claiming a consumer the tree contradicted. So the census states a POPULATION and a PARTITION with figures machine-derived by the derivation written here -- rerun it and the classes recount themselves -- and every symbol it names is one `git grep -n <symbol> -- src/v1 ':(exclude)src/v1/stage0'` finds. POPULATION: the lines of `grep -n` for the token Map inside double quotes over src/v1/*.dag -- 17 lines at this head, in five files: 04_infer.dag, 04_lookup.dag, 04_types.dag, 04_resolve.dag, 05_emit.dag. PARTITION, each line assigned by its enclosing symbol, disjoint and exhaustive (6 + 10 + 1 = 17): CLASS (a), SIX judgments that COMPARE the leaf spelling -- the probes. CLASS (b), TEN uses that SUPPLY the kernel container PROFILE name for Map: three in v1.compiler.infer_types bare_map_node and seven in make_map_type (container_param_name calls, the constructed node name, the profile-miss diagnostic pair). A profile constructor names the built-in it builds; it is not a judgment over authored text and cannot conflate two representations. CLASS (c), ONE line supplying a rendering fallback base name: v1.compiler.emit emit_map_type (”fallback_base: Map”, src/v1/05_emit.dag). THE SIX PROBES, and the EXECUTED EVIDENCE EACH ONE ACTUALLY HAS -- stated as it is, because the previous version of this receipt named RED tests that do not exist (probes 1 to 5 have none; the only witness tests on this branch are the four listed under probes 5 and 6 and the alias pair). (1) v1.compiler.infer classify_field_recursion, the MapValueRecursion match arm (src/v1/04_infer.dag) -- NO RED on this branch, and it is out of scope for the crossing branch for the reason stated at the end of this receipt; its evidence today is the field-shape witness for the recursion it shares with List and Set. (2) and (3) v1.compiler.infer expected_collection_surface, the join probe and the completion probe on the last name segment (src/v1/04_infer.dag) -- NO RED of their own; the joins they gate are covered from the outside by a_map_aliasing_the_keyed_algebra_joins_its_declaration_as_one_type in dag/test/claim/map_annotation_resolves_by_declaration_witness.dag. (4) v1.compiler.infer expected_type_is_keyed_collection, the arity-two-or-name test (src/v1/04_infer.dag) -- NO RED of its own. (5) v1.compiler.infer_lookup map_lookup_result_type, the authored_name_at test on the product node (src/v1/04_lookup.dag) -- NO RED of its own. (6) v1.compiler.infer_resolve unresolved_map_spelling_refusal, the bare-name test (src/v1/04_resolve.dag) -- added by THIS BRANCH, the subject of review 87479, and the one probe with executed look-alike evidence: a_lookalike_record_named_finitely_supported_function_aliased_as_map_is_not_the_kernel_container in dag/test/claim/map_annotation_resolves_by_declaration_witness.dag, plus the positive control an_imported_map_annotation_resolves_to_its_declaration and the fail-closed control a_map_annotation_without_an_import_refuses_as_unbound in the same file. Probe 6”s look-alike evidence lands where the decision is actually made, the alias settling in v1.compiler.types node_type_compatible, whose declared-container-alias arm returns the argument-by-argument all comparison with nothing after it (review 87307 removed two trailing disjuncts that had made it a silent widen; the_reviewer_named_element_type_pair_refuses_at_the_join in dag/test/claim/parameterized_alias_settles_by_declaration_witness.dag is the RED for that arm). PROBE 6 AT ONE CONSUMER, THE WAY REVIEW 87479 REQUIRED. `git grep -n unresolved_map_spelling_refusal -- src/v1 ':(exclude)src/v1/stage0' gives the definition and ONE call, inside unbound_container_diagnostics. unbound_container_diagnostics has one call site, in the keyed-collection arm of resolve_node_bounded whose guard is `let is_map = node_is_keyed_collection(n: n, source_indices: env.source_indices)` guard; the roster only CONCATENATES AN ERROR DIAGNOSTIC there. A roster line can refuse a name but can never RENDER a look-alike as the built-in. The earlier version of this row claimed that while is_user_generic_use_site was a second consumer; fixed by DELETION rather than patching -- the leaf-name gate this branch had added at that site is gone and the arm is byte-identical to main”s (`diff` of that arm against `git show origin/main:src/v1/04_resolve.dag`: equal), because the gate was itself the leaf-name key DESIGN 4 forbids at the one site that can route a use site to the kernel realization. The declaration_ref_eq helper that gate called was added by this branch and, once the gate went, had NO consumer at all: it is deleted with it, along with the two v1.compiler.infer_env import names it alone used, so the import list is again identical to main”s (DESIGN section 3c: a declaration nothing consumes is section 2”s redundant work in its purest form). Keying that arm on the declaration -- the other option the review offered -- was tried and rejected on evidence: FreeMonoid is declared in the CORPUS (dag/std/algebra.dag:154), so a declaration-identity test can answer ”this is the keyed algebra” for Map and FinitelySupportedFunction but cannot answer ”this is a built-in container” for List, Set or FreeMonoid, whose declarations are corpus-authored too; it would have made every authored FreeMonoid<T> a user generic. PROBE 6 IS A ROSTER, WHY, AND ITS RUNG: it fires exactly where the name resolves to NOTHING — the refusal is judged jointly with the module’s own visible-name set, so a module where the spelling DOES resolve to a declaration is excluded by that conjunct, by visibility rather than by the roster — and resolve sits BELOW the infer phase that resolves references and builds TypeEnv, so there is no resolved declaration node in hand to compare against. WHAT THE OTHER SIDE OF THE DECISION ACTUALLY DOES, STATED WITHOUT INFLATION: the keyed-container admission is node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling (src/v1/04_types.dag), and it compares container_template_algebra on the last segment of the authored name — a LEAF-SPELLING CHECK, not a declaration comparison. An earlier version of this row reported it as a declaration_ref_eq comparison; it is not one, and nothing on this branch compares declaration references at that decision. The RESIDUE note in v1.compiler.types already says the same. THE KERNEL-IDENTITY ADMISSION ITSELF IS MAIN’S (0f014468652c / PR #14880, an ancestor of origin/main); what this branch adds there is not a predicate but the DECLARATION that the spelling is the host realization, gunbc.design_ruling kernel_map_is_the_host_realization_of_the_finitely_supported_function. Probe 6”s next rung is named: give the resolve phase the declaration answer, and it stops being a roster question. TWO SPELLING KEYS SIT OUTSIDE THE POPULATION AND ARE NAMED SO NOTHING IS HIDDEN: is_container_type reads container_type_arity, the carrier roster deciding which names are containers at all (a name-membership question predating this PR and unchanged by it), and node_is_keyed_algebra_spelling, whose look-alike surface is the fsk.definer stand-in and the directly-spelled receiver a_directly_spelled_finitely_supported_function_receiver_dispatches_map_keys in dag/test/claim/fsf_spelling_resolves_as_kernel_keyed_container_witness.dag; hardening it to declaration identity is the next rung in gunbc.recurring_failure_mode emitter_keyed_container_lowering_is_keyed_by_leaf_spelling. THE SIX PROBES STAY OUT OF THE CROSSING BRANCH, AND THAT IS A DECLARED CEILING, NOT SILENCE: probes 1 to 5 carry no RED because retyping them is seed work outside the crossing, and six more seed judgment changes would widen the blast radius of a branch that must rebase over the ~110-module Map import wave. This row is the trigger that keeps them tracked.",





